  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nMain upper level trough axis will slowly move east across the \nregion this morning. Ahead of its passage, mid level cloud\nshield will gradually shift southeast, exiting the region around\nmidday. Areas of lower clouds associated with some lake\nmoisture/effect will also persist through mid morning,\nespecially across higher elevations of the SW Adirondacks,\nsouthern Greens and Berkshires. Spotty light sprinkles in valley\nareas, and sprinkles/flurries across higher elevations will also\npersist, especially upslope areas east of the Hudson River.\n\nSkies will then clear out this afternoon, first in valleys and\neventually across higher terrain areas. It will remain brisk\ntoday with northwest winds gusting to 25-35 mph at times,\nespecially through this morning. Temperatures will only reach\nthe mid/upper 40s in valley areas this afternoon, with mainly\n30s for higher terrain areas. Combined with the brisk wind, wind\nchill (\"Feels-Like\") temps will mainly be in the 30s in valleys,\nand 20s across higher elevations.\n\nClear skies and diminishing wind tonight amid a dry airmass\nshould allow temps to drop into the 20s for most areas, with a\nfew teens possible across the southern Adirondacks. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nHigh pressure should keep dry conditions across the region\nthrough midweek, with temps gradually moderating closer to\nseasonable levels, with daytime highs the upper 50s/lower 60s in\nmost areas. Nighttime lows will still be chilly given the\npotential for good radiational cooling, with lows mainly in the\n20s and 30s through midweek.",
